  <s:String x:Key="About.Title">ABOUT</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="About.Tagline">PBO &amp; GRAFT Packer for DayZ Modifications</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="About.Version">Version {0} · GRAFT {1}</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="About.Lead">PBOG Packer packs and signs DayZ mods. It packs client and server mods the way pboProject does; native server mods on the GRAFT framework it also builds from C++ and lays out as the GRAFT README says. One button takes you from the sources to a signed @mod and a ready start line.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="About.Features">What it does</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F1.T">My mods</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F1.D">Client, server and GRAFT mods in one list. Each has its own logo and status: whether it is built, which key signed it and which servers have it.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F2.T">One-click build</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F2.D">Client and server mods: binarized configs, rvmats and models, packing with AddonBuilder and signing with DSSignFile. The Grafted method adds the DLL build with clang-cl and CMake, graft protogen declarations, the grafted\ folder and the hid.dll host.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F3.T">Live log</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F3.D">The output of every tool in real time, a filter for warnings and errors, copying the log. A failed step shows a log excerpt, a hint and a retry from the same place.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F4.T">Environment</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F4.D">A toolchain check: clang-cl, CMake, Ninja, Windows SDK, AddonBuilder, CfgConvert, DSSignFile, graft.exe, hid.dll and the P: drive. Every problem comes with a ready command to fix it.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F5.T">Servers</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F5.D">DayZ server folders with the game version, the verifySignatures level and the GRAFT host status. One button installs the host or starts the server with its .bat file.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F6.T">Signing keys</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F6.D">Creates .bikey and .biprivatekey pairs, shows fingerprints, exports a key and lists the mods each key has signed.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F7.T">Start line</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F7.D">After the build the start line (-mod=@Name for a client mod, -serverMod=@Name for a server mod) and the full server start command are ready. The line goes to the clipboard by itself.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F8.T">EN, RU and UA</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="F8.D">The interface is in English, Russian and Ukrainian; the language switches on the fly without a restart.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="About.Thanks">Thanks</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="About.SeraphText">Thanks to the author and lead developer of GRAFT. Their work made C++ plugins for the DayZ server stable and accessible: finding engine entry points by the names of vanilla natives, the hid.dll host and the graft protogen declaration generator, which the whole PBOG Packer pipeline stands on.</s:String>
